{"type": "CompositeElement", "element_id": "04e627ab91d2f474bcbc180707df6a3b", "text": "IssueID_IssueKey:18889 MAP-597\n\nProjectID_Key:MAP Mapper\n\nIssueType:Sub\n\ntask\n\nStatus:Selected for Development\n\nPriority:{'self': 'https://nexefy.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/priority/2', 'iconUrl': 'https://nexefy.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/high.svg', 'name': 'High', 'id': '2'}\n\nAssigneeID_Name:62e3511d9e39d087ee5cceb1 lara\n\nReporterAdr_Name:james@nexefy.com James\n\nLabels:DESIGN\n\nComponents:\n\nUI Design for working across multiple frameworks\n\nFrom the story card -\n\nA user may have multiple frameworks they want to work with.\n\nThere are two types of frameworks. Industry frameworks that we create, and custom frameworks that users create.\n\nThis card covers the experience of how users navigate between and work with multiple frameworks. How we create the frameworks if covered elsewhere.", "metadata": {"data_source": {"record_locator": {"id": "18889", "key": "MAP-597", "board_id": null, "project_id": "MAP"}, "date_created": "2025-03-28T01:45:50.066+0000", "date_modified": "2025-03-28T01:46:55.121+0000", "date_processed": "1744461415.3862824"}, "filename": "18889.txt", "filetype": "text/plain", "languages": ["eng"], "orig_elements": ""}}